  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Team Europe Renewable Hydrogen Fund Chile</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Team Europe Green Hydrogen Fund for Chile is a joint initiative by the European Investment Bank (EIB) and the German KfW Development Bank (KfW), led by the Delegation of the European Union in Chile to promote the incipient green hydrogen market in Chile, foster local supply chains, and strengthen the potential for green hydrogen exports to Europe, while considering the importance of a just energy transition.The project is embedded in the Team Europe Initiative (TEI) on Green Hydrogen Development in Chile, which aims at supporting the decarbonisation ofthe Chilean economy, creating green jobs, and generating business opportunities for Chilean and European companies, whilst contributing to meet the EU&#xbf;s demand for import of green hydrogen.</narrative>
  </description>
